SUMMARY:Yoga In Nature™\, NCMA 
DESCRIPTION:Yoga In Nature™\, NC\n**September is National Yoga Month\, a
 nd I welcome you to join us outdoors\, in nature\, for a slower vinyasa fl
 ow to yin** **practice** ending in savasana. **ALL LEVELS and those new to
  yoga welcome!** Join our community and meet other like-minded people!\n\n
 *Rain date\, if needed\, will be Sunday\, Sept. 6 at 9am.*\nPractice vinya
 sa flow yoga at North Carolina Museum of Art\, outdoors near upper parking
  area in grass ellipse... (NOTE THIS GRASS LOCATION\, as there are other g
 roups that use NCMA grounds). WHEN YOU COME INTO THE PARKING LOT\, DRIVE T
 O WHERE THE TWO PARKING LOTS ON BLUE RIDGE MEET\, AWAY FROM THE MUSEUM. We
  practice in the grass Ellipse area:)\n$15/person\nCash\nVenmo @Darlene-Ge
 nander (0862)\nPaypal dgenander@yogainnature.com\n\nPlease bring your yoga
  mat or large towel\, water\, sunscreen and insect repellent (if you use).
  Optional: a plastic reusable liner for under your mat (to protect it if g
 round is wet/damp) or towel.
